WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.088
An IaC repository is not just a place to
store text.

2
00:00:05.168 --> 00:00:11.940
It may define production networks, access
policies, storage locations,

3
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:18.901
databases, compute resources, logging
pipelines, encryption settings,

4
00:00:18.981 --> 00:00:21.166
and security controls.

5
00:00:21.246 --> 00:00:26.598
A repository change can become an
infrastructure change,

6
00:00:26.678 --> 00:00:33.887
so the repository itself becomes a control
point that deserves protection and

7
00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:34.732
review.

8
00:00:34.812 --> 00:00:41.038
Pull requests, branch protection, code
owners, required reviews,

9
00:00:41.118 --> 00:00:43.630
signed commits where used,

10
00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:51.684
and protected environments all help ensure
infrastructure changes are intentional.

11
00:00:51.764 --> 00:00:59.192
These controls create a reviewable path
from proposed change to applied change.

12
00:00:59.272 --> 00:01:06.481
A production apply should not happen
merely because someone changed a file in a

13
00:01:06.561 --> 00:01:13.770
low-trust context or because a workflow
was triggered by an unreviewed event.

14
00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:17.455
Pipelines add another trust boundary.

15
00:01:17.535 --> 00:01:23.433
A runner may receive credentials, read
state, calculate plans,

16
00:01:23.513 --> 00:01:29.411
comment on proposed changes, or apply
infrastructure updates.

17
00:01:29.491 --> 00:01:32.441
That runner is not just compute.

18
00:01:32.521 --> 00:01:39.511
It is an execution environment with access
to the automation control plane.

19
00:01:39.591 --> 00:01:45.708
Its permissions, workspace handling,
secrets, logs, artifacts,

20
00:01:45.788 --> 00:01:48.519
and trigger rules all matter.

21
00:01:48.599 --> 00:01:55.371
Secure design separates untrusted triggers
from privileged execution.

22
00:01:55.451 --> 00:02:02.879
A pull request from an untrusted source
may be allowed to run limited validation,

23
00:02:02.959 --> 00:02:09.731
but it should not automatically receive
credentials capable of changing

24
00:02:09.811 --> 00:02:11.449
infrastructure.

25
00:02:11.529 --> 00:02:18.411
Production environments should use
protected branches, protected tags,

26
00:02:18.491 --> 00:02:24.389
explicit approvals, and environment gates
where appropriate.

27
00:02:24.469 --> 00:02:31.460
The path from request to plan to apply
should remain visible and reviewable.
